@*
    The build stamp (YYMMDD), bottom-right on every page, and the site's contentinfo landmark.

    2026-11-17, owner decision: the version is visible again on every page. It had been
    reduced to a screen-reader-only footer; the fleet standard wants the build date readable
    at a glance (bug reports, "am I on the new build?"). It sits above the BottomNav on a
    phone and above the modal layer, so the first-visit initials prompt cannot hide it.
    pointer-events: none keeps it from ever taking a tap meant for the page.
*@
<footer class="app-build-footer" aria-label="Site information">
    <span class="gl-sr-only">PoMiniGames, build @BuildInfo.Date</span>
    <span class="app-build-version" data-testid="build-version" aria-hidden="true">v@(BuildInfo.Date)</span>
</footer>
